> **Corpus placement** — This standalone document is canonically synthesized in [`B5 — Ethics, Stewardship, and Governance`](../../Synthesis Project/B5 — Ethics, Stewardship, and Governance.ormd#reverent-stewardship "meta:corresponds_to"). Relational Volition: how agency and choice are relational rather than isolated properties. Canonical treatment in B5 §1–§2.

# Executive Summary: Relational Volition {#summary-header}

This document provides a synthesis of the proposal that human agency is a systems-level property rather than a metaphysical exception to natural law. By integrating [E² (Essence of Existence)](#abstract "meta:corresponds_to") and [CFA (Constraint-Fluctuation-Attention)](#cfa-dynamics "ontological:composes") dynamics, the original text establishes [Relational Volition (Vᵣ)](#definition-vr "ontological:defines") as a measurable capacity for a system to navigate its environment while maintaining field integrity.

## 1. Redefining Agency {#redefining-agency}

The traditional concept of "free will" is deconstructed into relational functions where [will and freedom](#definition-vr "meta:emerges_from") are seen to [emerge from](#definition-vr "meta:emerges_from") the interaction of nested systems. Key classical terms are mapped to relational equivalents:

- **Freedom** is redefined as the [Constraint Gradient (∇C)](#components "meta:corresponds_to"), representing mobility within field boundaries.
- **Will** is mapped to the [Attentional Vector (Â)](#components "meta:corresponds_to"), the directional bias that modulates the field.
- **Moral Agency** becomes [Coherence Responsibility (Φ_res)](#components "meta:corresponds_to"), the duty to preserve the integrity of the containing system.

## 2. The Mechanics of Volition {#mechanics}

Within the [CFA model](#cfa-dynamics "ontological:composes"), [Volition](#summary "dynamical:interacts_with") operates through [attention’s selective amplification of fluctuation](#cfa-dynamics "dynamical:transforms_to"). This process does not override the laws of the field; rather, it utilizes [Attention as field modulation](#summary "ontological:defines") to achieve [local navigation](#summary "dynamical:transforms_to") within the [field geometry](#summary "symmetric:constrains") established by [Determinism](#summary "symmetric:constrains"). 

[Relational Volition (Vᵣ)](#definition-vr "ontological:defines") is thus the ability to steer within [Boundary geometry](#summary "symmetric:constrains") by engaging with [Micro-level fluctuation potential](#summary "dynamical:interacts_with") without causing systemic collapse.

## 3. Ethical Implications and Stewardship {#ethics-summary}

The framework [supports](#ethics "epistemic:supports") the philosophy of [Reverent Stewardship](#ethics "epistemic:supports"), where freedom is characterized as the [capacity for coherence-preserving navigation](#summary "meta:emerges_from"). In this view, responsibility is the [Maintenance of field integrity](#summary "epistemic:supports").

## 4. Conclusion {#conclusion-summary}

To exercise true volition is to [act coherently](#conclusion "symmetric:preserves") within the laws of relational emergence. Freedom is found in the ability to [sustain pattern integrity](#conclusion "ontological:defines") and [preserve the generative capacity](#conclusion "epistemic:supports") of the relational fields we inhabit.